## Context

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged reports solely by normalized subject.
The [reassessment of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-reassessment) finds that the incident's own computed
cause table separates a shared-parser defect from a booking-v3 hint defect. The live triage
explorer also compares causes rather than subjects. The old accepted record is preserved;
this proposal replaces its operational rule for the reassessment, pending desk acceptance.

## Decision

Use matching subjects to find candidates, not as evidence of a common problem. Look up the tenant's
locale and booking-form version and inspect the entry channel and symptom. For the exported date
classifier, merge only when `sameCause` establishes a non-null common cause. Keep parser and hint
reports in separate issues even when their subjects match. Different subjects do not justify
splitting reports when their cause is established to be the same.

Unknown tenants and contradictory symptoms need investigation, not automatic merging. In
particular, retain the timing anomalies as unresolved evidence rather than claiming that their
filing category proves their root cause. Deduplicate export overlap by report ID before counting.

